 ```
 
+## Staged updates
+
+Transfer and activation can be separated when the reboot window is not the
+transfer window. `stage` validates the package, transfers the image into the
+inactive slot, and verifies the device-side digest. No candidate slot is
+selected and the device is never rebooted, so it keeps running its confirmed
+firmware. `activate` later finishes the update from the journal record alone.
+
+```sh
+fwctl --device sensor-0042 stage sensor-node-1.2.0.fwpkg
+fwctl staged
+fwctl --device sensor-0042 activate
+```
+
+One record is kept per device in `staging_file`; staging again replaces it.
+`activate` consumes the record whatever the outcome and refuses to move boot
+state when the device no longer matches the record on product, running version,
+rollback counter, held transfer, or accepted bytes.
+
 After an update, run `fwctl --device sensor-0042 history` to review the outcome
 recorded locally, or `fwctl doctor` if a device does not show up in `fwctl
 devices`.
